Sval: notify a refused camera, microphone or screen request

`prompt` denies a camera, microphone or screen request whose permission is
blocked for the site and tells nothing else, so the page fails with no sign
in the browser. Sval's site controls show that attempt (`SvalSiteControls`),
so the denial notifies `sval-webrtc-blocked` with the browser and the
permission id.

diff --git a/browser/actors/WebRTCParent.sys.mjs b/browser/actors/WebRTCParent.sys.mjs
index d97d92add2..191baba914 100644
--- a/browser/actors/WebRTCParent.sys.mjs
+++ b/browser/actors/WebRTCParent.sys.mjs
@@ -550,6 +550,7 @@ function prompt(aActor, aBrowser, aRequest) {
       lazy.SitePermissions.getForPrincipal(principal, permissionID, aBrowser)
         .state == lazy.SitePermissions.BLOCK
     ) {
+      Services.obs.notifyObservers(aBrowser, "sval-webrtc-blocked", permissionID);
       aActor.denyRequest(aRequest);
       return;
     }
